# Documentation Maintenance

- Keep docs short and true. Prefer updating existing docs over new ones.
- Per product: `README.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/security.md`, `docs/decisions/` (ADRs only when consequential), `.env.example`.
- Tiny: usually no doc change. Normal+: update architecture (and README if setup/commands change) when behavior or boundaries change. Sensitive: also refresh security assumptions.
- Do not leave architecture docs stale after a main-flow change.
- Detail: `standards/documentation.md`.
